 death. \nThe *Historical Records* of Raymond III's life and reign are limited but it is known that he was a significant figure in the history of the Crusader states. \nHe was a member of the House of Toulouse and played a key role in the *Defense of the County of Tripoli*. \nThe *Battle of Hattin* in 1187 was a significant defeat for the Kingdom of Jerusalem and marked the beginning of the end of the Crusader states. \nRaymond III was not present at the battle but his county was affected by its outcome. \nThe *Siege of Tripoli* in 1188 was a significant event in the *Later Life* of Raymond III and marked the end of his reign as Count of Tripoli. \nHe was a skilled military leader and played a key role in the *Defense of the County of Tripoli* but was ultimately unable to defend his county against the Muslim states of the region. \nThe *Count of Tripoli* was a significant title in the Kingdom of Jerusalem and Raymond III was the last Count of Tripoli from the House of Toulouse. \nHe played a key role in the *Politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem* and was a prominent figure in the history of the Crusader states. \nThe *Kingdom of Jerusalem* was a significant power in the region during the 12th century and Raymond III played a key role in its defense. \nHe was a skilled military leader and was able to defend his county against several attacks but was ultimately unable to defend the Kingdom of Jerusalem against the Muslim states of the region.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -2.9802276912960224e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009116546134464443}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00020203932945150882}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.2074330747127533}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.49049508571624756}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.072883037